  "conversion_adaptations": [
    "Final independently re-evaluates all three public workloads together with three hidden same-distribution workloads.",
    "Calibration-driven alignment to the author BATCHS parallel branch and representative graph scale was adopted. The source-locked reference uses CountWorkEfficientParallelTotal/CountOrigCompactParallelTotal while the independent baseline uses the frozen serial dispatch.",
    "Continuous score is independent of the pass/fail reference and has no finite upper clipping; raw timing and speedup measurements are retained.",
    "Formal answering is 18000 seconds and independent final evaluation is 1800 seconds; model requests are 64 MiB and audit bundle allowance is 8 GiB.",
    "Beat spec v3 (2026-10-07): each suite adds one deterministic Chung-Lu graph with power-law degrees on both sides, where vertex ranking decides the wedge count; uniform graphs, metrics and the 1.05 rule are unchanged; train verifier-wall budget 30000 -> 40000 s for the fourth development graph.",
    "Reference f-metric selection (2026-10-12): the source-locked reference no longer computes the requested ACOCORE ranking unconditionally on the BATCHS path; CountTotal applies the paper's Section 6.2.2 runtime rule, using side ordering when (ws - wr)/ws < 0.1 for degree-order wedge count wr and degree ordering otherwise. Only apps/hyper/butterfly_count_total.h differs from upstream; workloads, metrics, the 1.05 rule, the serial oracle path and the frozen baseline are unchanged."
  ],
